    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Four railroad lines were built in Dallas County in 1881, one surveyed by Samuel Fordyce, sparking Fordyce's growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fordyce%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fordyce became Dallas County's largest town by 1890 and was selected as the county seat in 1908.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://yacosa.net/fordyce-ar-history-population-economy-attractions-and-more/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Dallas County Courthouse, built in the early 1900s, remains one of Fordyce's most recognizable landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
